coder › Implemented `compareSemver(a, b)` in `src/semver.ts` and added tests in `src/semver.test.ts`, on branch `work/compare-semver` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/semver.ts`: strict semver regex parser (no leading zeros, no `v` prefix, required `major.minor.patch`, valid prerelease/build chars); `major/minor/patch` compared numerically; release > prerelease; prerelease identifiers compared one-by-one (numeric numerically, alphanumeric lexically via ASCII `<`, numeric < alphanumeric, shorter list lower on prefix); build metadata (`+...`) parsed but ignored. Invalid input throws `TypeError: Invalid semantic version: "<input>"`.
- `src/semver.test.ts`: 9 tests covering numeric core comparison, prerelease < release, the semver.org precedence chain, numeric/alphanumeric identifier rules, shorter-list rule, build-metadata ignored, and TypeError naming the bad string (both arguments).

Decisions not in the brief:
- ASCII lexical comparison for alphanumeric identifiers (semver §11.4.4); hyphen sorts before letters/digits accordingly.
- Numeric prerelease comparison is length-then-lexical (exact beyond `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`) — valid since the regex already rejects leading zeros.
- Error message format: `Invalid semantic version: "<version>"` (names the string inside quotes, so empty string is still visible).

